{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The current best is config_009 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.635 accuracy. The architecture components—multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion—are well-supported by the evidence (avgpool > transformer by ~5 pts; weighted ≥ concat; multiprofile >> singleprofile; imagenet_vit_l > resnet50 at similar cost). The main untested variable that could push accuracy higher is the RNA encoder: scgpt was clearly worse (0.512), but scvi_n200 (a learned variational encoder) has not been paired with the best image/fusion stack. config_032 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) directly tests whether a learned RNA representation can outperform PCA while keeping all other parameters at their proven-optimal settings. This is a focused exploitation of the strongest configuration with one targeted change. Expected cost is moderate (~5–8 GPU hours), comparable to config_009 (7.02 h) since scvi_n200 is a learned encoder similar in complexity to scgpt (4.33 h in config_021), keeping total budget well within limits for the remaining 2 experiments."
}

